  "rules": {
    "oracle": "{T}: Add {C}.\n{1}: This land becomes a 1/1 Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying until end of turn. It's still a land.\n{1}, {T}: Target Blinkmoth creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.",
    "cr": [
      "205.3m",
      "205.1b",
      "305.7",
      "611.2a",
      "613.1d",
      "613.1f",
      "702.9b"
    ],
    "actual": "phase-rs's coverage report lists the card as unsupported with the gap `ParserMisfire:InvalidSubtype(Blinkmoth)`.",
    "expected": "{1}: until end of turn it becomes a 1/1 Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying that is still a land (CR 305.7, 611.2a). {1}, {T}: target Blinkmoth creature (CR 205.3m) gets +1/+1 until end of turn.",
    "diagnosis": "`coverage::check_subtype_lexicon` (game/coverage.rs:8125) flags every `AddSubtype` whose value isn't in `collect_valid_subtypes` (game/coverage.rs:7919), and that lexicon is built only from the subtypes printed on card type lines. No card prints Blinkmoth on its type line (it only appears in become effects and in Blinkmoth Nexus's own pump), so the real creature type Blinkmoth (CR 205.3m; it is in the engine's own crates/engine/data/oracle-subtypes.json) is reported as a parser misfire. The parsed abilities are exactly the Oracle text, and the sandbox games show them working.",
    "suggested_fix": "Build the coverage lexicon from the full CR 205.3 subtype list the engine already ships (crates/engine/data/oracle-subtypes.json, via database::subtype_vocab) in addition to printed type lines, so a real subtype that only appears in rules text (Blinkmoth; probably others like it) isn't a ParserMisfire. Keep flagging tokens that aren't subtypes at all (\"Gets\", \"Until\"), which is what the check is for.",
    "override_note": "Nothing is patched: the test ops pin the animation's modifications (1/1, flying, artifact and creature types, Blinkmoth subtype; the separate \"still a land\" step keeps the land type) and the pump's Blinkmoth-creature target filter, as verified. The sandbox games show it as printed: animated it's an artifact (Shatter can target it), still a land (Stone Rain can), a 1/1 flier that attacks for 1; the next turn it's only a land; the pump has no target until a Blinkmoth creature exists (a Grizzly Bears isn't one) and then makes the Nexus 2/2."
  },
